{"step_index":176,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-23T20:10:01Z","thinking":"**Initiating Project Generation**\n\nI'm now diving into the problem seeder and dataset generator, as planned! It seems the initial request is for CodeDuel to launch with a curated collection of 1,000 significant coding problems. Currently, I'm focusing on the problem distribution, starting with 120 problems related to arrays and hashing. I'll get that problem set compiled, then broaden the scope.\n\n\n**Defining Problem Distributions**\n\nThe problem categories are now concretely defined, and I've established the target quantities for each: Two Pointers & Sliding Window (80), Binary Search (70), Strings (70), Linked List (60), Stacks/Queues (90), Trees (100), Heap (50), Greedy (60), Backtracking (40), Graphs (120), Dynamic Programming (130), Bit Manipulation (40), Trie (20), and Advanced DSA (50). This distribution sums to 1,000 problems, and has a balanced difficulty. Now, I will start by designing the `ProblemSeeder.java` and `ProblemDataGenerator.java` to fulfill database population.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"package com.codeduel.seed;\\n\\nimport com.codeduel.model.*;\\nimport com.codeduel.repository.AchievementRepository;\\nimport com.codeduel.repository.ProblemRepository;\\nimport com.codeduel.repository.TestCaseRepository;\\nimport com.codeduel.repository.UserRepository;\\nimport org.slf4j.Logger;\\nimport org.slf4j.LoggerFactory;\\nimport org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Value;\\nimport org.springframework.boot.CommandLineRunner;\\nimport org.springframework.security.crypto.password.PasswordEncoder;\\nimport org.springframework.stereotype.Component;\\nimport org.springframework.transaction.annotation.Transactional;\\n\\nimport java.time.LocalDateTime;\\nimport java.util.*;\\n\\n@Component\\npublic class ProblemSeeder implements CommandLineRunner {\\n\\n    private static final Logger log = LoggerFactory.getLogger(ProblemSeeder.class);\\n\\n    private final ProblemRepository problemRepository;\\n    private final TestCaseRepository testCaseRepository;\\n    private final UserRepository userRepository;\\n    private final AchievementRepository achievementRepository;\\n    private final PasswordEncoder passwordEncoder;\\n\\n    @Value(\\\"${codeduel.seeder.enabled:true}\\\")\\n    private boolean seederEnabled;\\n\\n    public ProblemSeeder(ProblemRepository problemRepository,\\n                         TestCaseRepository testCaseRepository,\\n                         UserRepository userRepository,\\n                         AchievementRepository achievementRepository,\\n                         PasswordEncoder passwordEncoder) {\\n        this.problemRepository = problemRepository;\\n        this.testCaseRepository = testCaseRepository;\\n        this.userRepository = userRepository;\\n        this.achievementRepository = achievementRepository;\\n        this.passwordEncoder = passwordEncoder;\\n    }\\n\\n    @Override\\n    @Transactional\\n    public void run(String... args) {\\n        if (!seederEnabled) {\\n            log.info(\\\"Problem seeder is disabled.\\\");\\n            return;\\n        }\\n\\n        seedUsers();\\n        seedAchievements();\\n\n<truncated 24036 bytes>","Description":"\"ProblemSeeder component that initializes the 1,000 question bank, users, and achievements\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\rajan\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\codeduel\\\\backend\\\\src\\\\main\\\\java\\\\com\\\\codeduel\\\\seed\\\\ProblemSeeder.java\"","toolAction":"\"Creating ProblemSeeder.java\"","toolSummary":"\"Write ProblemSeeder\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
